{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387948-how-would-garou-react-to-the-child-of-a-ronin","id":1387948,"title":"How would Garou react to the child of a Ronin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-13T00:58:09-07:00","id":1387948,"title":"How would Garou react to the child of a Ronin?","content":"Say a werewolf is kicked out of their tribe for whatever reason. This now-Ronin has a child who is also a Garou, as many Ronin surely do. If this child experiences their First Change and their Ronin parent isn't around anymore (dead or otherwise no longer in the picture), what would then happen to the child? Would their parent's former tribe be willing to claim them or would they just end up becoming a lost cub? <br /> <br /> I can see four main scenarios happening:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The tribe decides it has nothing to do with the child. After all, they kicked the parent out of the tribe, so their child obviously isn't a tribe member either.</li> <li>The tribe watches and waits to see whether the child is worth claiming as one of theirs (however, this has all the dangers associated with lost cubs)</li> <li>A lost cub is trouble for everyone - the tribe decides to claim the child (or passes them off to a tribe that isn't picky about adopting lost cubs)</li> <li>The tribe is unaware that this child even exists in the first place (seems unlikely, as I remember reading somewhere that tribes tend to keep tabs on their former members)</li> </ol><br /> I'm guessing it'd depend on the tribe as to whether they'd intervene (I'd say Bone Gnawers would probably adopt/claim such pups, for example), but is there any official WtA material that says what would happen in this sort of situation? If not, what do you all think would happen?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26161-urbansentinels","name":"UrbanSentinels","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T03:11:12-07:00","id":1387970,"title":"","content":"I'd assume most cubs of Ronin end up as Lost Cubs by default, esp. if their Ronin parent is out of the picture. The Tribes aren't exactly tracking every Ronin's movements to know where they are or what they're up to; esp. male Ronin since them having kids is generally easier to miss. Most Ronin are kept track of because they can't completely be free of the Garou Nation. They need to find some Sept that will tolerate them being nearby, and has some members willing to trade so the Ronin can get access to things they're going to need.<br /> <br /> Purebreed is certainly going to play a factor here. For Tribes with it, a Ronin's kid that still has their breeding is worth at least trying to adopt and bring into the fold for that alone.<br /> <br /> The majority of the Tribes will adopt... so while the stigma of having a Ronin parent is a thing (assuming anyone even knows), you don't need to be born into a Tribe to become a member of it. It might be an up-hill battle with lots of negative social issues to deal with, but a child of the Get of Fenris could decide to seek initiation into the Fianna if Stag's Tribe felt where they belonged. Some Tribes are, of course, far more adoption willing than others. Even if the cub of a Ronin can't find a place in their parent's Tribe, the Children of Gaia or Bone Gnawers are quite likely to let them in.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, there are cultural issues against. A Ronin Red Talon that has a Homid kid? Well that kid isn't getting into the Red Talons. Similarly with the Black Furies and any male Garou kids one of their Ronin might birth.<br /> <br /> Generally, there's really two main scenarios: The cub ends up with their familial Tribe despite whatever caused their parent to become a Ronin, or the cub ends up in one of the Tribes that tend adopt Garou struggling to find acceptance in the other Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T23:47:47-07:00","id":1388248,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd say a &quot;lost cub&quot; is a garou who by the time of the first change is unaware of garou society. If the parent is Ronin and became Ronin recently, this might not be the case.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd think it makes a difference, if the child was born before or after the garou in question was banned from the tribe and who the other parent is.<br /> <br /> In any case, there isn't so much &quot;the tribe&quot; as an authority, there is only the garou of the Ronin's former sept. It his their behaviour and mind set that influences what happens.<br /> Are they keeping an eye on the Ronin? Possibly, especially if the Ronin remains within the area the sept's packs usually consider their turf. If that is the case, they would gain knowledge of the child and possibly claim it by means of the 'baptism of fire'. If the member's of the parent's tribe within the sept decide against that, for whatever reason, garou of more welcoming tribes, like the children of gaia, black furies and bone gnawers might claim the child.<br /> Also, the child's grandparents, uncle/aunts, cousins and especially the other parent, if so called kenning (human) kinfolk, might influence what happens, and might advocate for an integration of the child into the tribe.<br /> <br /> As of W20 the Rite to determine ancestry that was formerly presented in TB: Get of Fenris rev. is iirc described as a general tool to all tribes. So, if at least some garou in the sept that finds the child care, the parentage might not be a secret for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}